                    },
                    "message": "It would be a good improvement to write unit tests for this function, and I don't think too complicated. Would just need to add the prototype to the header so the testcase can use it.  Would you be in a position to do that?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "phosphor-rsyslog-config/server-conf.cpp",
                    "line": 39,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Palaniappan Arunachalam",
                        "email": "palaniappana@ami.com",
                        "username": "Palaniappanarunachalam"
                    },
                    "message": "If parseConfig() is made tolerant to comments and blank lines, but\nwriteConfig() rewrites the file into a single line and removes everything else,\nare we intentionally not preserving existing content?\n\nWhat's the expected behavior here?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "phosphor-rsyslog-config/server-conf.cpp",
                    "line": 39,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "Agreed.  writeConfig() would just overwrite anything."
                },
                {
                    "file": "phosphor-rsyslog-config/server-conf.cpp",
                    "line": 44,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Palaniappan Arunachalam",
                        "email": "palaniappana@ami.com",
                        "username": "Palaniappanarunachalam"
                    },
                    "message": "By accepting comments, you're saying \"it's okay to manually edit this system-generated file.\"? why would someone want to edit the system generated file?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "phosphor-rsyslog-config/server-conf.cpp",
                    "line": 44,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Meghana Vangapandu",
                        "email": "meghanav@ami.com",
                        "username": "MeghanaVangapandu0"
                    },
                    "message": "This change is not to encourage manual edits of a system-managed file. It makes restore parsing more robust when comment or blank lines appear before the forwarding rule (for example from provisioning/config tooling).\n\nPreviously, parsing assumed the rule was on the first line, which could cause restore to fall back to defaults. This fix skips comment/blank lines and parses the first valid entry, while keeping the file management model unchanged."
                }
            ],
